<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
  <!--
    MAIN EXECUTABLE ONLY (package.json build.mac.entitlements). Every other
    Mach-O in the bundle - the Electron helpers, the python seed, uv, node-pty's
    spawn-helper - is signed with build/entitlements.mac.inherit.plist instead.

    Two keys are deliberately ABSENT here, and the release gate
    (scripts/verify-macos-artifacts.mjs, app-hardening-entitlements, policy in
    src/shared/macos-entitlement-policy.json) refuses a bundle that carries them:

    - com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables: with it, any
      same-uid process could DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES into the genuine signed app
      and run code that still satisfies the app's designated requirement
      (measured in the F2 spike: a dylib constructor ran in the signed process
      with cs_flags unchanged). The runtime's app-signature attestation means
      nothing while that holds.
    - com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation: main loads only code
      signed by our team (Electron Framework, node-pty's pty.node, all re-signed
      at package time), so library validation passes without it, and keeping it
      would let a planted dylib load into the signed process.

    allow-jit and allow-unsigned-executable-memory stay: V8 needs them.
    Design: F2 "card answers verified by the app's code signature".
  -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.files.bookmarks.app-scope</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.files.downloads.read-write</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.microphone</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.screen-capture</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
